01/ed-1/seq-2/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_houseleek_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743555:1866070101:0260/199,1291,952,238/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "The export of specie by this day's\nsteamers aggregated $433,854, of which the Germania\ntook $200,000, the City of New York $78,642, the New\nYork $68,212 and the Lafayette $87,000, making for the\nweek $550,574.", "lineage_id": "herald:L6758659144b31830", "source": "herald"}, {"mark": "11", "claim": "Brought news from Panama, to 1866-07-01", "citation": "Evening Star (Washington), 9 July 1866, p. 2, col. 2", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83045462/1866-07-09/ed-1/seq-2/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_leonberger_ver03:data:sn83045462:00280654279:1866070901:0077/1073,836,1034,146/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "The steamship New\nYork, from Aspinwall, with Panama[?] dates to\nthe 1st inst., has arrived.", "lineage_id": "star:Lf86978227f5265a3", "source": "star"}], "aboard": {"specie": [{"text": "$3,840", "marks": ["‡"]}, {"text": "$68,212", "marks": ["10"]}], "passengers": [{"n": 92, "marks": ["‡"]}], "mails": [{"text": "55 bags", "marks": ["‡"]}], "headlines": [{"text": "FROM CENTRAL AND SOUTH AMERICA", "dates_to": "1866-07-01", "marks": ["11"]}], "mail": []}}